@startuml
!include https://static.visual-paradigm.com/web/resources/plantuml-stdlib/themes/vp.puml

title Chat - Chat with Seller

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam activityFontName Arial
skinparam activityFontSize 14
skinparam activityBorderThickness 1.5
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam ArrowColor #222222
skinparam SwimlaneBorderColor #222222
skinparam SwimlaneBorderThickness 2
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #7DD3FC
  BorderColor #2563EB
  DiamondBackgroundColor #7DD3FC
  DiamondBorderColor #2563EB
  StartColor #111827
  EndColor #FFFFFF
}

|Customer|
start
note right
Precondition:
The customer is signed in.

Postcondition:
The message is stored once (idempotency key) and pushed
to both participants. The other side's messages are
marked read when the conversation is opened.
end note
:Choose to message the seller from a product, shop or order;
|System|
:Find this pair's conversation or create it;
if (The other participant is unknown or invalid?) then (Yes)
  :Return the not-found error;
  |Customer|
  :View the message;
  stop
else (No)
endif
|System|
:Display the messages, newest first, and mark the other side's messages read;
|Customer|
repeat
:Enter the text or choose an image;
:Send the message;
|System|
if (The system fails while processing the request?) then (Yes)
  :Return the system error;
  |Customer|
  :View the system error;
  stop
else (No)
endif
|System|
:Check there is content or an image on the project's Cloudinary, an idempotency key, and that the sender is a participant;
backward :Return the send error;
repeat while (The message is empty, the\nimage is not allowed, the key\nis missing or the sender is\nnot a participant?) is (Yes) not (No)
:Save the message; a reused key returns the stored message;
:Push the message to both sides over WebSocket after commit;
|Customer|
:View the new message;
stop

@enduml
